  "faq_title": "Frequently asked questions",
  "faq_items": [
    {
      "q": "How do I get a serial?",
      "a": "Open a doctor's profile, choose a day to see which chambers are open, and tap Call for booking. The chamber gives you your serial number and when to arrive."
    },
    {
      "q": "Do I pay online?",
      "a": "No. Cura doesn't take payments. You pay the doctor's consultation fee at the chamber, as usual."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I cancel my serial?",
      "a": "Call the chamber to cancel, so they can give the serial to someone else. Serials booked online earlier can still be cancelled from My appointments."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I know a doctor is genuine?",
      "a": "Each profile shows the doctor's BMDC registration number, so you can check it with the Bangladesh Medical & Dental Council."
    },
    {
      "q": "What should I do in an emergency?",
      "a": "Cura is not an emergency service. Call 999 for an ambulance or urgent help, or 16263 (Shasthya Batayon) for free medical advice — both are available 24/7."
    },
    {
      "q": "Is Cura live yet?",
      "a": "Not yet — this is a demo build. Doctors and hospitals are sample data and no real appointment is created, so please don't enter real medical details."
    }
  ],
